                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d512cb96-7a73-3c7b-a6fe-f8515f456660",
                        "entry_id": "6d90816a-ae60-3e46-93ba-4d8fa01f4055",
                        "glosses": [
                            "past passive perfective participle of вы́трезвить (výtrezvitʹ)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of",
                            "participle",
                            "passive",
                            "past",
                            "perfective"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a3bb55a-c28a-43ee-a98c-d86685cb0de3",
                                "sense_id": "d512cb96-7a73-3c7b-a6fe-f8515f456660",
                                "text": "Я заме́тил тут не́сколько ли́чностей чуть не в про́рванных сюртука́х, в са́мых сомни́тельных, сли́шком не в ба́льных костю́мах, очеви́дно вы́трезвленных с непоме́рным трудо́м и на ма́лое вре́мя, и бог зна́ет отку́да взя́тых, каки́х-то иногоро́дних.",
                                "translation": "I noticed several personages there in all but torn frock coats, in the most dubious and utterly un-ball-like outfits, who had obviously been sobered up with boundless effort and for a short time only, and had been fetched from God knows where, perhaps from out of town.",
                                "english": "I noticed several personages there in all but torn frock coats, in the most dubious and utterly un-ball-like outfits, who had obviously been sobered up with boundless effort and for a short time only, and had been fetched from God knows where, perhaps from out of town."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
